import NagataBlueprint.Prelude

open Verso.Genre
open Verso.Genre.Manual
open Informal

#doc (Manual) "Blow-ups and admissible centres" =>

:::group "grp:blowups"
The blow-up of a quasi-coherent ideal sheaf, built chart by chart from the Rees algebra and
glued over the base, together with the calculus of admissible centres: universal property,
products, finite-degree descent, composition, extension across a quasi-compact open,
density, and the two boundary constructions.
:::

# The blow-up of a quasi-coherent ideal sheaf

:::definition "def:affine-blowup" (parent := "grp:blowups") (lean := "AlgebraicGeometry.reesGrading, AlgebraicGeometry.reesMonomial, AlgebraicGeometry.reesGradingZero, AlgebraicGeometry.reesX, AlgebraicGeometry.AffineBlowup, AlgebraicGeometry.AffineBlowup.toSpec, AlgebraicGeometry.AffineBlowup.chart, AlgebraicGeometry.AffineBlowup.awayAlgebraMap")
For an ideal $`I` of a commutative ring $`A`, the Rees algebra $`\bigoplus_n I^n` carries a
grading whose degree-one part contains the Rees element attached to each element of $`I`.
The _affine blow-up_ is $`\Proj` of that graded ring, with its structure morphism to
$`\Spec A` and its affine charts at the degree-one Rees elements.
:::

:::definition "def:blowup" (parent := "grp:blowups") (lean := "AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.blowupFunctor, AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.blowupNatTrans, AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.blowupGluingData, AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.blowup, AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.blowupMap, AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.blowupι, AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.isPullback_blowupι")
For a quasi-coherent ideal sheaf $`\sI` on a scheme $`X`, the affine blow-ups over the affine
opens of $`X` glue along the localizations of the Rees algebras
{uses "def:affine-blowup"}[]. The resulting scheme is the _blow-up_ $`\Bl_\sI(X)`, with its
structure morphism $`\pi_\sI \colon \Bl_\sI(X) \to X` and its chart open immersions from the
affine blow-ups, whose comparison squares over the affine opens are cartesian.
:::

:::theorem "thm:blowup-proper" (parent := "grp:blowups") (lean := "AlgebraicGeometry.AffineBlowup.isProper_toSpec, AlgebraicGeometry.finiteType_reesGrading_zero, AlgebraicGeometry.AffineBlowup.toProjectiveSpace, AlgebraicGeometry.AffineBlowup.isClosedImmersion_toProjectiveSpace, AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.isProper_blowupMap")
If $`\sI` is of finite type, then $`\pi_\sI \colon \Bl_\sI(X) \to X` is proper.
:::

:::proof "thm:blowup-proper" (uses := "def:blowup, def:finite-type-ideal")
Properness is local on the target, so it suffices to treat an affine blow-up at a finitely
generated ideal. There the Rees algebra is generated in degree one by finitely many
elements, so the affine blow-up is a closed subscheme of a projective space over the base,
and the degree-zero part is of finite type.
:::

:::theorem "thm:blowup-principalization" (parent := "grp:blowups") (lean := "AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.isInvertible_comap_blowupMap, AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.isEffectiveCartierCenter_subschemeι_comap_blowupMap, AlgebraicGeometry.AffineBlowup.map_awayAlgebraMap_reesX_eq_span_singleton, AlgebraicGeometry.AffineBlowup.isRegular_awayAlgebraMap_reesX")
The inverse image ideal sheaf $`\sI \cdot \sO_{\Bl_\sI(X)}` is invertible: on the chart at a
degree-one Rees element it is generated by that element, which is a nonzerodivisor.
:::

:::theorem "thm:blowup-iso-complement" (parent := "grp:blowups") (lean := "AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.isIso_blowupMap_restrict, AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.isIso_blowupMap_restrict_support_compl, AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.isIso_blowupMap_of_isInvertible, AlgebraicGeometry.AffineBlowup.isIso_toSpec_of_isRegularPrincipal, AlgebraicGeometry.AffineBlowup.isIso_toSpec_of_eq_top")
The blow-up morphism restricts to an isomorphism over the open complement $`V(\sI)^{c}` of
the centre; more generally, blowing up an invertible centre is an isomorphism
{uses "def:blowup"}[].
:::

# Admissible centres

:::definition "def:admissible" (parent := "grp:blowups") (lean := "AlgebraicGeometry.IsAdmissible, AlgebraicGeometry.IsAdmissible.preservedOpen")
Let $`X` be a scheme and $`U \subseteq X` an open. A $`U`-admissible _centre_ is a
quasi-coherent ideal sheaf $`\sI` on $`X` which is of finite type and whose support is
disjoint from $`U`; equivalently, $`\sI` restricts to the unit ideal on $`U`. The associated
$`U`-admissible _blow-up_ is $`\pi_\sI \colon \Bl_\sI(X) \to X` {uses "def:blowup"}[]. We
write $`\mathrm{pr}(\sI) = V(\sI)^{c}` for the _preserved open_; it contains $`U`.
:::

:::proposition "prop:admissible-basic" (parent := "grp:blowups") (lean := "AlgebraicGeometry.IsAdmissible.isProper_blowupMap, AlgebraicGeometry.IsAdmissible.isIso_blowupMap_restrict")
A $`U`-admissible blow-up is proper, and it restricts to an isomorphism over the preserved
open, in particular over $`U` {uses "def:admissible"}[].
:::

:::proof "prop:admissible-basic" (uses := "thm:blowup-proper, thm:blowup-iso-complement")
Both statements are the finite-type case of the corresponding property of an arbitrary
blow-up.
:::

:::theorem "thm:0806" (parent := "grp:blowups") (lean := "AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.exists_lift_blowup, AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.hom_ext_of_isInvertible_comap, AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.exists_lift_blowup_comap, AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.hom_ext_comap_blowup")
Let $`\sI` be a quasi-coherent ideal sheaf on $`X` and let $`t \colon T \to X` be a morphism
such that $`\sI \cdot \sO_T` is invertible. Then $`t` factors through $`\pi_\sI`, and the
factorization is unique: two morphisms $`T \to \Bl_\sI(X)` over $`X` agree as soon as
$`\sI \cdot \sO_T` is invertible.
:::

:::proof "thm:0806" (uses := "def:blowup, def:affine-blowup")
The statement is local on the charts of the blow-up, where it reduces to the universal
property of the chart ring $`A[\sI/a]`: for a ring map $`\varphi \colon A \to R` with
$`\varphi(a)` a nonzerodivisor dividing the extension of $`\sI`, the assignment
$`x/a^n \mapsto` the unique solution of $`y \varphi(a)^n = \varphi(x)` is a well-defined ring
map, and ring maps out of a chart ring which agree on the base and have regular value on the
chart denominator coincide. Uniqueness globalizes through the localization describing the
overlap of two charts.
:::

:::theorem "thm:080A" (parent := "grp:blowups") (lean := "AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.exists_blowup_mul_iso, AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.exists_blowup_mul_isInvertible_iso, AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.exists_blowup_mul_iso_of_comap_eq")
For quasi-coherent ideal sheaves $`\sI, \sL` on $`X` there is an isomorphism over $`X`
$$`\Bl_{\sI \cdot \sL}(X) \;\cong\; \Bl_{\sL \cdot \sO_{\Bl_\sI(X)}}\bigl(\Bl_\sI(X)\bigr).`
Moreover multiplying a centre by an invertible ideal sheaf does not change the blow-up.
:::

:::proof "thm:080A" (uses := "thm:0806, thm:blowup-principalization")
On the iterated blow-up the inverse image of $`\sI \cdot \sL` is invertible, which produces a
morphism in one direction; on $`\Bl_{\sI \cdot \sL}(X)` the inverse images of $`\sI` and of
$`\sL` are invertible, because a factor of an invertible product ideal is invertible, which
produces lifts in the other direction; the two composites are identities by uniqueness of
lifts.
:::

:::theorem "thm:0803" (parent := "grp:blowups") (lean := "AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.exists_finiteDegree_center_le_blowup, AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.exists_finiteDegree_center, AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.blowupChart, AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.chartIdeal, AlgebraicGeometry.AffineBlowup.chartFrac")
Let $`X` be quasi-compact quasi-separated, let $`\sI` be a finite-type centre on $`X` and let
$`\sJ` be a finite-type ideal sheaf on $`\Bl_\sI(X)`. Then there are an integer $`d \ge 1`
and a finite-type ideal sheaf $`\sL \le \sI^{d}` on $`X` with
$$`\sL \cdot \sO_{\Bl_\sI(X)} \;=\; \bigl(\sI \cdot \sO_{\Bl_\sI(X)}\bigr)^{d} \cdot \sJ.`
:::

:::proof "thm:0803" (uses := "thm:01PF, def:blowup, thm:blowup-principalization")
The argument is organised around the maximal degree-$`d` candidate. Over an affine open of
the base, the blow-up is covered by the charts at the degree-one elements of a finite
generating set of the centre; each generator of the chart ideal of $`\sJ` is cleared into a
numerator lying in the $`d`-th power of the centre and having the prescribed fraction in
_every_ chart of the same algebra. A finite-type subsheaf through these finitely many
numerators is then extracted by the extension theorem, and it generates the required product
chart by chart.
:::

:::theorem "thm:080B" (parent := "grp:blowups") (lean := "AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.exists_blowup_comp, AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.exists_blowup_comp_base_change, AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.coe_support_eq_of_comap_pow_mul")
Let $`X` be quasi-compact quasi-separated, let $`\sI` be a finite-type centre on $`X` and let
$`\sJ` be a finite-type centre on $`\Bl_\sI(X)`. Then there is a finite-type centre $`\sK` on
$`X` with
$$`V(\sK) = V(\sI) \cup \pi_\sI\bigl(V(\sJ)\bigr)`
and an isomorphism $`\Bl_\sK(X) \cong \Bl_\sJ(\Bl_\sI(X))` compatible with the structure
morphisms to $`X`.
:::

:::proof "thm:080B" (uses := "thm:0803, thm:080A")
Let $`\sL` be the finite-degree descent of $`\sJ` and put $`\sK = \sI \cdot \sL`. The product
formula identifies $`\Bl_\sK(X)` with the blow-up of $`\sL \cdot \sO_{\Bl_\sI(X)}`; removing
from the latter its invertible exceptional factor identifies it with
$`\Bl_\sJ(\Bl_\sI(X))`. The support formula is read off from the same descent.
:::

:::corollary "cor:080L" (parent := "grp:blowups") (lean := "AlgebraicGeometry.IsAdmissible.exists_comp, AlgebraicGeometry.IsAdmissible.mul")
Let $`X` be quasi-compact quasi-separated and $`U \subseteq X` an open. The composite of a
$`U`-admissible blow-up $`\pi_1 \colon X_1 \to X` with a $`\pi_1^{-1}U`-admissible blow-up
$`X_2 \to X_1` is again a $`U`-admissible blow-up of $`X`: there are a $`U`-admissible centre
$`\sK` on $`X` and an isomorphism $`X_2 \cong \Bl_\sK(X)` under which the composite becomes
$`\pi_\sK` {uses "def:admissible"}[].
:::

:::proof "cor:080L" (uses := "thm:080B")
Apply the composition theorem and read off from the support formula that the resulting
centre is again disjoint from $`U`.
:::

:::lemma_ "lem:blowup-restrict" (parent := "grp:blowups") (lean := "AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.exists_isPullback_blowup_comap, AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.exists_blowup_comap_iso, AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.exists_comm_lift_blowup_comap_opens, AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.nonempty_arrowIso_morphismRestrict_lift_blowup, AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.nonempty_arrowIso_morphismRestrict_lift_blowup_of_comap_eq, AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.isOpenImmersion_morphismRestrict_lift_blowup_congr")
For an open immersion $`O \to X` and a quasi-coherent ideal sheaf $`\sI` on $`X`, the blow-up
of $`\sI|_O` is the restriction of $`\Bl_\sI(X)` over $`O`, the comparison square being
cartesian. Consequently the canonical lift $`\Bl_{\sI \cdot \sO_Y}(Y) \to \Bl_\sI(X)`
attached to a morphism $`Y \to X` localizes on the base, and two centres agreeing over an
open have isomorphic lifts there {uses "def:blowup"}[].
:::

:::theorem "thm:080M" (parent := "grp:blowups") (lean := "AlgebraicGeometry.IsAdmissible.exists_extend, AlgebraicGeometry.IsAdmissible.exists_extend_of_disjoint, AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.exists_finiteType_comap_eq_of_disjoint")
Let $`X` be quasi-compact quasi-separated, let $`W \subseteq X` be a quasi-compact open, let
$`U \le W` be an open and let $`\sJ` be a finite-type centre on $`W` whose support is
disjoint from $`U`. Then there is a $`U`-admissible centre $`\sI` on $`X` together with a
morphism $`\Bl_\sJ(W) \to \Bl_\sI(X)` over $`W \to X` making the square cartesian; that is,
the blow-up of $`\sI` restricts over $`W` to the blow-up of $`\sJ`.
:::

:::proof "thm:080M" (uses := "thm:01PF, thm:01PH, lem:blowup-restrict")
Extend $`\sJ` to a finite-type ideal sheaf on $`X` and multiply it by a finite-type ideal
cutting out the boundary of $`W`; the product is $`U`-admissible, and blow-up formation
commutes with restriction to an open subscheme.
:::

# Density along admissible blow-ups

:::theorem "thm:admissible-density" (parent := "grp:blowups") (lean := "AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.IsInvertible.isSchemeTheoreticallyDominant_compl_support, AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.isSchemeTheoreticallyDominant_blowupMap_preimage_compl_support, AlgebraicGeometry.IsAdmissible.isSchemeTheoreticallyDominant_preimage_ι, AlgebraicGeometry.IsAdmissible.dense_coe_preimage_preservedOpen, AlgebraicGeometry.IsAdmissible.dense_preimage_blowupMap, AlgebraicGeometry.IsAdmissible.dense_coe_preimage_blowupMap, AlgebraicGeometry.IsAdmissible.dense_preimage_blowupMap_of_qcqs, AlgebraicGeometry.IsAdmissible.isNoetherian_blowup")
Let $`\sI` be a quasi-coherent ideal sheaf on $`X`.

* If $`\sI` is invertible, the open complement of its support is scheme-theoretically dense.
* The inverse image of $`V(\sI)^{c}` in $`\Bl_\sI(X)` is scheme-theoretically dense, the
  inverse image of the centre being invertible.
* If $`U` is a quasi-compact scheme-theoretically dense open of $`X`, its inverse image under
  a $`U`-admissible blow-up is scheme-theoretically dense.
* The inverse image of a dense subset of a quasi-compact quasi-separated scheme under an
  admissible blow-up is dense.
:::

:::proof "thm:admissible-density" (uses := "thm:blowup-principalization, def:admissible")
The first item is local: an invertible ideal is locally generated by a nonzerodivisor, whose
non-vanishing locus is schematically dense. The second follows by principalization on the
blow-up, and the last two by combining the first two with the isomorphism over the preserved
open.
:::

:::theorem "thm:dense-admissible-exists" (parent := "grp:blowups") (lean := "AlgebraicGeometry.exists_isAdmissible_isSchemeTheoreticallyDominant_preimage, AlgebraicGeometry.IsAdmissible.exists_comp_isSchemeTheoreticallyDominant_preimage")
Let $`X` be quasi-compact quasi-separated and $`U \subseteq X` a quasi-compact open. Then
there is a $`U`-admissible blow-up of $`X` in which the inverse image of $`U` is
scheme-theoretically dense; one blows up a finite-type centre supported exactly on
$`X \setminus U`. The same holds dominating a prescribed $`U`-admissible blow-up $`B`: apply
the absolute form on the total space of $`B` and compose the two blow-ups.
:::

:::proof "thm:dense-admissible-exists" (uses := "thm:01PH, thm:admissible-density, cor:080L")
Blow up a boundary ideal, use that the preserved open is then exactly $`U`, and compose with
a prescribed admissible blow-up when one is given.
:::

# Separating boundary pieces

:::definition "def:separation-blowup" (parent := "grp:blowups") (lean := "AlgebraicGeometry.separationBlowup")
For quasi-coherent ideal sheaves $`\sI_1, \sI_2` on $`X`, the _separation blow-up_ is the
blow-up of the sum $`\sI_1 \sqcup \sI_2` {uses "def:blowup"}[].
:::

:::theorem "thm:0F3V" (parent := "grp:blowups") (lean := "AlgebraicGeometry.disjoint_range_strictTransformMap_sup")
Let $`X` be quasi-compact quasi-separated and let $`\sI_1, \sI_2` be finite-type
quasi-coherent ideal sheaves. Then the strict transforms of the closed subschemes
$`V(\sI_1)` and $`V(\sI_2)` along the separation blow-up of $`\sI_1 \sqcup \sI_2` have
disjoint ranges.
:::

:::proof "thm:0F3V" (uses := "def:separation-blowup, def:strict-transform")
The charts of $`\Bl_{\sI_1 \sqcup \sI_2}(X)` at degree-one elements coming from local
sections of $`\sI_1` or of $`\sI_2` cover the blow-up. On a chart attached to a section of
$`\sI_i` the extended centre is generated by that section, so the strict transform of
$`V(\sI_i)` misses that chart entirely; hence the two strict transforms cannot meet.
:::

:::theorem "thm:080Y" (parent := "grp:blowups") (lean := "AlgebraicGeometry.exists_admissibleBlowup_cartierBoundary, AlgebraicGeometry.exists_admissibleBlowup_cartierBoundary_of_coe_support_eq_compl, AlgebraicGeometry.exists_admissibleBlowup_cartierBoundary_of_isLocallyNoetherian")
Let $`X` be quasi-compact quasi-separated and $`U \subseteq X` a quasi-compact open. Then
there is a $`U`-admissible blow-up $`\pi \colon X' \to X` and an invertible ideal sheaf
$`\sJ` on $`X'` whose support is exactly the complement of $`\pi^{-1}U`. On a locally
Noetherian scheme the same holds for an arbitrary open $`U`.
:::

:::proof "thm:080Y" (uses := "thm:01PH, thm:blowup-principalization, def:admissible")
Blow up a finite-type centre supported exactly on $`X \setminus U`; its inverse image is
invertible with the required support.
:::
